{"family": "memflow", "task": "flow", "name": "MemFlow", "plain": "MemFlow (Dong and Fu, CVPR 2024): optical flow with a motion memory, a RAFT-style network whose update step also reads attention over the frame's motion features. Apache-2.0 code and weights; some training sets are research-only.", "summary": "MemFlow (Dong & Fu, CVPR 2024): optical flow with a memory of past motion. A RAFT-style network at 1/8 resolution: BasicEncoder feature and context networks, an all-pairs correlation pyramid, a motion encoder and update block of depthwise-separable large-kernel blocks (SKFlow) instead of a GRU, and an attention readout of the motion features of memory frames; convex 8x upsampling. The authors' released weights; the network is ported from DQiaole/MemFlow. A pair (image1, image2) runs as upstream's first frame of a video (empty memory: the readout attends over the pair's own motion features). Paper (video with memory, val_decoder_depth 15): Sintel test EPE 1.05 (clean) / 1.91 (final), KITTI 2015 test Fl-all 4.10 %.", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/DQiaole/MemFlow", "upstream_commit": "5486fb88a55b04c2e2b292b3abaa7641d9988831", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "MemFlow: Optical Flow Estimation and Prediction with Memory", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.04808", "date": "2024-04-07", "venue": "CVPR 2024", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["raft_flow"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "iters", "default": 15, "bounds": ">= 1", "effect": "output"}], "outputs": [{"name": "flow", "extra": false}], "output_info": {}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": ["Pairs only: the video memory (the keys and values of earlier frames that upstream's inference keeps) is not exposed; each pair runs as the first frame of a video.", "The MemFlow-T checkpoints (Twins-SVT encoders) and MemFlow-P (flow prediction) are not ported."], "task_io": "Input: two RGB images (consecutive frames). Output: per-pixel motion from the first to the second (dx, dy in pixels).", "install": {"extras": [], "noncommercial_weights": []}, "variants": [{"id": "memflow", "released": null, "added_in": "0.2.0", "ref": "memflow@1", "name": "memflow", "setting": "", "default_tag": false, "params": {}, "licence": {"code": "Apache-2.0", "code_class": "permissive", "weights": "Apache-2.0", "weights_assumed": false, "evidence": "https://github.com/DQiaole/MemFlow/blob/5486fb88a55b04c2e2b292b3abaa7641d9988831/LICENSE", "training_data": [{"id": "flyingchairs", "name": "FlyingChairs (Freiburg)", "licence": "LicenseRef-research-only", "commercial": "no", "url": "https://lmb.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/resources/datasets/FlyingChairs.en.html"}, {"id": "sceneflow", "name": "Freiburg SceneFlow (FlyingThings3D, Driving, Monkaa)", "licence": "LicenseRef-research-only", "commercial": "no", "url": "https://lmb.informatik.uni-freiburg.de/resources/datasets/SceneFlowDatasets.en.html"}], "training_note": "FlyingThings3D (part of SceneFlow), starting from SKFlow's FlyingChairs + FlyingThings3D checkpoint, as upstream's train.sh", "commercial": "yes", "reasons": [], "notes": ["data: flyingchairs (non-commercial)", "data: sceneflow (non-commercial)"]}, "weights": [{"name": "MemFlowNet_things.pth", "sha256": "694cc33c1ac5945798aaf001e7b26a7966a01873879b6d03e5f3d54c97e28d36", "size": 25400354, "url": "https://github.com/DQiaole/MemFlow/releases/download/v1.0.0/MemFlowNet_things.pth", "host": "GitHub", "member": null, "archive_size": null, "mirror": null}], "input_size": "any H x W >= 128, padded to a multiple of 8", "tested_max": {"size": "1024x2048", "alloc_mib": 8440, "reserved_mib": 9462}, "speed": {"standard": "1080x1920", "inputs": [{"input": "375x1242", "scene": "synthetic", "standard": false, "modes": {"portable": {"ms": 143.798, "ms_min": 143.553, "noise": 0.00